      "statusChangeNewStatus": "closed",
      "value": "Thanks for the report but this is actually known and expected behavior. All controllers now get the SteamVR hand skeleton applied (in the same way that Index controllers previously could move fingers even with gestures disabled). SteamVR creates estimated skeletal motion even for Quest controllers and that's what you're seeing now.\n\nWe received feedback that some people want to go back to the old behavior so there is a new toggle in the Main Menu - Controls page that you can use to turn off the SteamVR finger tracking applying to your avatar called \"Avatars Use Finger Tracking\" - once turned off your avatar will go back to only using animations for hands and not using the skeletal tracking.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-08-13T05:34:57.987Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "It's odd because it isn't like normal gestures that are still working, expressions are locked however I can still wiggle my fingers but it's sort of scuffed. It's almost like it's trying to do hand tracking even tho I have my controllers on.",
